  "evidence": [
    "Coordinator expands this existing immutable Texture ownership scope to 61F0D0 pointer inputs and its retained61F785 fragment:61F1AE/61F1C2/61F1C6 loads a leading pixels-pointer cell;61F1BC publishes remap base, later DWORD reads use byte selector times four;61F1B7 publishes full lookup base,61F4C0..61F4CA performs byte-offset DWORD reads. No producer-side shade class or table extent is established. Recover minimal pointer contracts, retain original arithmetic, ABI stack width, guard/read order, mappings and fragment parent symbol; do not assert nominal Texture input ownership or pixel-loop acceptance from a setup-only host control.",
    "Pinned Texture::extract 619710..6198DE publishes allocator byte-buffer results to receiver+0, copies width bytes per row with owned width or borrowed 256 destination pitch. Constructor, close/destructor and all pixel users are owned in texture.cpp.",
    "Pinned draw_trans 6198E0 publishes receiver+0 at619910 then samples bytes at619D20. Source consumers consistently use unsigned byte texels. Replace opaque void* member with unsigned char* without retyping shared raster scratch, numeric target-width addressing or ownership flags.",
    "Preserve borrowed/owned allocation/free semantics and the destructor pointer-clear store. Use a same-type volatile pointer view instead of aliasing the member through void**; retain historical mappings/claims and all offset/layout facts.",
    "Baseline d91b0f103: fresh build-dutv3i79 passes; ignored buffer-pixel-address-current-oct10.json includes 96 Texture verdicts. Exactness and full-game fidelity remain separate obligations. Existing actual-source mutation controls must continue proving late pixel publication, source/shade distinction, row pitch and borrow behavior."
  ],
  "intent": "Recover the byte-pixel member type across Texture storage lifecycle and all sampling consumers",
